module iemSensorDetection
module sawLysingDetection
module miR21FreefloatingDetection
module miR21TotalDetection

manifest Plasma_Sample
manifest PBS_1x
manifest PBS_4x
manifest PBS_01x
manifest TAE_Buffer_10x
manifest miR21_OligoProbe
manifest SAW_Actuator
manifest IEM_AEM_Sensor
manifest IEM_CEM_Concentrator

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Extracellular Vesicle microRNA Quantification from Plasma
// Using an Integrated Microfluidic Device
// Ramshani et al., Communications Biology (2019) 2:189
// DOI: 10.1038/s42003-019-0435-1
//
// Protocol: PCR-free absolute quantification of free-floating
// and EV-contained miR-21 from untreated human plasma using
// (1) a surface acoustic wave (SAW) lysing chip that
//     mechanically lyses EVs under continuous flow, and
// (2) a concentration/sensing chip with ion-exchange
//     membranes (IEMs) that concentrate and detect
//     target miRNA via current-voltage curve (CVC) shift.
//
// Biomarker: miRNA hsa-mir-21-5p (miR-21)
//   Sequence: TAGCTTATCAGACTGATGTTGA
//   Correlation: pancreatic cancer, lung cancer,
//                colorectal cancer, hepatocellular carcinoma.
//
// Key specs:
//   Sample volume   : ~20 uL per measurement (40 uL total)
//   Assay time      : ~30 min per measurement (~60 min total)
//   Detection limit : 1 pM
//   Quantification  : <10% uncertainty (absolute, PCR-free)
//   SAW frequency   : 28 MHz, 1 W
//   SAW flow rate   : 250 uL/h
//   EV lysis time   : ~1 min in SAW channel
//   Concentration V : 200 V DC for 20 min
//   Hybridisation   : 20 min (concurrent with concentration)
//   Wash buffer     : 4x PBS (post-hybridisation)
//   CVC buffer      : 0.1x PBS (measurement)
//
// NOTE ON IEM SENSOR ABSTRACTION:
//   The AEM sensor is functionalized with a complementary
//   ssDNA oligoprobe (TCAACATCAGTCTGATAAGCTA) to miR-21.
//   Target hybridisation shifts the over-limiting region of
//   the CVC by Delta-V (V), which is log-linearly correlated
//   to miR-21 concentration:
//     C (nM) = exp((Delta-V - 0.76145) / 0.06614)
//   `detect iemSensorDetection` abstracts the CVC sweep
//   (Gamry 500 potentiostat, Ag-AgCl reference electrodes).
//   `detect sawLysingDetection` abstracts SAW actuation
//   and confirms lysis before downstream sensing.
//   `detect miR21FreefloatingDetection` abstracts CVC shift
//   measurement for the unlysed (free-floating) plasma run.
//   `detect miR21TotalDetection` abstracts CVC shift
//   measurement for the SAW-lysed (total miRNA) plasma run.
//
// NOTE ON CONCENTRATION STEP ABSTRACTION:
//   Application of 200 V DC across the CEM reservoir for
//   20 min creates an ion-depletion zone upstream of the
//   AEM sensor, concentrating negatively charged miRNA
//   by up to three orders of magnitude directly beneath
//   the sensor where hybridisation occurs. This is modelled
//   as a `heat` step at 25c (room temperature) for 20 min
//   (= 1200 s), reflecting the ambient temperature of the
//   concentration/sensing chip during IEM operation.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                  -- device setup, IEM baseline CVC,
//                                  free-floating miR-21 measurement
//   BB2  freefloatingPass      -- freefloatSignal > 0: valid
//                                  free-floating miR-21 detected;
//                                  proceed to SAW-lysed total run
//   BB3  freefloatingFail      -- freefloatSignal <= 0: no signal
//                                  (below sensor limit); drain
//   BB4  freefloatingJoin      -- join: total miRNA measurement begins
//   BB5  totalPass             -- totalSignal > 0: valid total miR-21
//                                  (free-floating + EV-miRNA) detected;
//                                  dispose and compute EV fraction
//   BB6  totalFail             -- totalSignal <= 0: no total signal;
//                                  drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup          -- terminal: dispose QC signals,
//                                  experiment ends
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prepare 1x PBS running buffer and establish
//         baseline CVC on the IEM sensor (oligoprobe only,
//         no sample). The sensor is functionalized prior to
//         use with miR-21 complementary ssDNA oligoprobe
//         (TCAACATCAGTCTGATAAGCTA) via standard amine-
//         coupling on the AEM surface.
//         This baseline CVC (miR-21 probe in 1x PBS only)
//         is used as the reference for all Delta-V measurements.
//         Buffer volume: 60 uL (used as driver fluid after
//         sample injection throughout the protocol).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

runningBuffer   = dispense 1 units of PBS_1x
probeBaseline   = dispense 1 units of IEM_AEM_Sensor

baselineMix     = mix runningBuffer with probeBaseline for 5s
baselineSignal  = detect iemSensorDetection on baselineMix for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: MEASUREMENT 1 - Free-floating miR-21 quantification.
//         ~20 uL of untreated human plasma is injected into
//         the integrated platform with the SAW device OFF
//         (no EV lysis). The sample passes through the lysing
//         chip channel and flows directly into the
//         concentration/sensing chip.
//         Flow rate: 250 uL/h (sample + 60 uL PBS driver).
//         The SAW chip channel is bypassed acoustically
//         (IDT powered off) -- EVs remain intact.
//         Only free-floating miR-21 present in plasma reaches
//         the IEM sensor.
//         NOTE: `mix` here abstracts continuous flow injection
//         through the microfluidic channel; no DMF-style
//         droplet merging occurs. Plasma is used as-is with
//         no sample preparation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

plasmaRun1      = dispense 1 units of Plasma_Sample
driverBuffer1   = dispense 1 units of PBS_1x

// Continuous-flow channel injection (SAW OFF - no lysis).
// Flow carries 20 uL plasma + 60 uL PBS driver at 250 uL/h.
channelFlow1    = mix plasmaRun1 with driverBuffer1 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: IEM concentration - apply 200 V DC across CEM
//         reservoir for 20 min. The resulting depletion zone
//         concentrates negatively charged free-floating
//         miR-21 upstream of the AEM sensor surface.
//         Hybridisation with the oligoprobe occurs
//         concurrently during this 20-min window.
//         Modelled as room-temperature incubation (25 C,
//         20 min = 1200 s) to represent non-thermal IEM
//         electrokinetic concentration at ambient conditions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cemConcentrator1 = dispense 1 units of IEM_CEM_Concentrator
concentrating1   = mix channelFlow1 with cemConcentrator1 for 1200s

// IEM electrokinetic concentration at ambient temperature.
heat concentrating1 at 25c for 1200s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Post-hybridisation wash with 4x PBS to remove
//         non-hybridised species from the AEM sensor surface.
//         Then pump 0.1x PBS into the channel prior to the
//         CVC measurement sweep.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

washBuffer1     = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
washed1         = mix concentrating1 with washBuffer1 for 2s

cvcBuffer1      = dispense 1 units of PBS_01x
readyForCVC1    = mix washed1 with cvcBuffer1 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: CVC sweep - measure Delta-V for free-floating
//         miR-21. Concentration voltage is terminated;
//         Gamry 500 potentiostat applies current-voltage
//         sweep (0 to 2.5 V) between the AEM sensor reservoir
//         and upstream reservoir via platinum electrodes.
//         Voltage drop measured by Ag-AgCl reference electrodes
//         across the sensor. Delta-V in the over-limiting
//         current region is recorded.
//         miR21FreefloatingDetection abstracts this CVC sweep
//         and returns a positive signal if Delta-V > sensor
//         noise floor (> ~0.1 V for free-floating miR-21
//         in healthy human plasma as per paper Fig. 3).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freefloatSignal = detect miR21FreefloatingDetection on readyForCVC1 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Free-floating miR-21 QC gate
// Pass (BB2): freefloatSignal > 0 -> measureable Delta-V
//             detected for free-floating miR-21; dispose
//             and proceed to SAW-lysed total measurement.
// Fail (BB3): freefloatSignal <= 0 -> signal below sensor
//             noise floor (< 1 pM); drain and abort.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (freefloatingJoin).
// ============================================================

if (freefloatSignal > 0) {
    dispose readyForCVC1
} else {
    drain readyForCVC1
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: freefloatingJoin
// Dispose free-floating QC signal. Control falls into
// total miRNA measurement branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose freefloatSignal
dispose baselineSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: MEASUREMENT 2 - Total miR-21 quantification
//         (free-floating + EV-contained miR-21).
//         A fresh 20 uL aliquot of the same plasma sample is
//         injected with the SAW device ACTIVE (28 MHz, 1 W).
//         SAWs refract into the polycarbonate microchannel
//         perpendicular to the IDT array, generating acoustic
//         pressure that mechanically shears EVs open.
//         Residence time: ~1 min in the SAW channel at
//         250 uL/h flow rate -- sufficient for ~100% EV lysis.
//         Released EV-miRNA and free-floating miRNA both
//         flow into the concentration/sensing chip.
//         NOTE: `mix` abstracts SAW channel flow-through.
//         sawLysingDetection confirms acoustic lysis before
//         the lysate enters the IEM chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sawActuator     = dispense 1 units of SAW_Actuator
plasmaRun2      = dispense 1 units of Plasma_Sample
driverBuffer2   = dispense 1 units of PBS_1x

// SAW lysis: 28 MHz, 1 W, ~1 min exposure at 250 uL/h.
// NOTE: `mix` abstracts the channel-flow EV lysis event.
// No DMF electrode mixing occurs; this models acoustic
// pressure shearing of EV membranes under continuous flow.
sawLysate       = mix plasmaRun2 with sawActuator for 60s

// Detect lysis completion (confirms EVs are mechanically
// disrupted before lysate enters concentration/sensing chip).
lysisSignal     = detect sawLysingDetection on sawLysate for 10s

// Flow lysate into concentration/sensing chip under PBS driver.
channelFlow2    = mix sawLysate with driverBuffer2 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: IEM concentration - second run.
//         200 V DC applied for 20 min across CEM reservoir.
//         Both free-floating miR-21 and EV-released miR-21
//         (total pool) concentrate upstream of the AEM sensor
//         and hybridise with the miR-21 oligoprobe.
//         IEM sensor is replaced (disposable) between runs
//         to maintain optimised repeatability.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cemConcentrator2 = dispense 1 units of IEM_CEM_Concentrator
concentrating2   = mix channelFlow2 with cemConcentrator2 for 1200s

// IEM electrokinetic concentration at ambient temperature.
heat concentrating2 at 25c for 1200s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Post-hybridisation wash and buffer exchange
//         for the total miRNA CVC measurement.
//         4x PBS wash removes non-hybridised species.
//         0.1x PBS is pumped in before the CVC sweep.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

washBuffer2     = dispense 1 units of PBS_4x
washed2         = mix concentrating2 with washBuffer2 for 2s

cvcBuffer2      = dispense 1 units of PBS_01x
readyForCVC2    = mix washed2 with cvcBuffer2 for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: CVC sweep - measure Delta-V for total miR-21
//          (free-floating + EV-miRNA).
//          Same potentiostat procedure as STEP 6.
//          Expected Delta-V for total miR-21 in healthy human
//          plasma: ~0.65-0.7 V (vs ~0.1 V for free-floating
//          only) as per paper Fig. 3.
//          The difference in voltage shift between Measurement
//          1 (free-floating) and Measurement 2 (total)
//          directly quantifies the EV-miR-21 fraction.
//          EV-miR-21 concentration is calculated from the
//          calibration curve: C = exp((Delta-V - 0.76145) / 0.06614)
//          miR21TotalDetection abstracts this CVC sweep and
//          returns positive signal if Delta-V significantly
//          exceeds the free-floating baseline (> ~0.2 V shift
//          from free-floating run expected for EV contribution).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

totalSignal     = detect miR21TotalDetection on readyForCVC2 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Total miR-21 QC gate
// Pass (BB5): totalSignal > 0 -> measurable Delta-V for
//             total miR-21 detected; Delta-V > free-floating
//             signal confirming EV-miRNA released by SAW.
//             Dispose all droplets and proceed to cleanup.
// Fail (BB6): totalSignal <= 0 -> no total signal (SAW lysis
//             failure or IEM sensor issue); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (totalSignal > 0) {
    dispose readyForCVC2
    dispose lysisSignal
} else {
    drain readyForCVC2
    drain lysisSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// The EV-miR-21 expression level is computed off-chip by
// comparing the two voltage shifts using:
//   ExpressionLevel = exp((Delta-V_total - Delta-V_freefloat) / b)
// where b = 0.06614 is the log-linear calibration fitting
// parameter from the IEM sensor calibration curve (Fig. 2b).
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose totalSignal
dispose baselineMix

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
